1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:35,307 --> 00:01:37,977
So that's the port town Pazzio!

17
00:01:52,317 --> 00:01:55,487
Looks like there's lots of delicious foods here.

18
00:01:55,487 --> 00:01:56,157
Hey!

19
00:01:57,307 --> 00:02:00,167
Shouldn't you hide your face?

20
00:02:00,167 --> 00:02:02,077
What's <i>that</i> supposed to mean?

21
00:02:02,077 --> 00:02:04,127
If you've lived in the village for hundreds of years,

22
00:02:04,127 --> 00:02:06,797
won't there be some folktales about your human form?

23
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:15,757
"Holo occasionally makes an appearance in the village in the form of a beautiful girl of about fifteen."

24
00:02:16,207 --> 00:02:23,397
"She has long, flowing hair, the ears of a wolf, and a splendid, dark brown, white-tipped tail."

25
00:02:23,397 --> 00:02:28,147
"She promises a plentiful harvest in return for keeping her appearance a secret."

26
00:02:28,147 --> 00:02:30,217
Then they know exactly what you look like!

27
00:02:30,617 --> 00:02:34,007
You doubted my identity, and so would others.

28
00:02:34,377 --> 00:02:37,647
Only seeing my ears or tail would make them take a second glance.

29
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,747
You might be right.

30
00:02:40,747 --> 00:02:42,327
There's no chance.

31
00:02:42,707 --> 00:02:45,157
I've been long forgotten.

32
00:02:47,187 --> 00:02:49,827
That's all I can ask for as far as I'm concerned.

33
00:02:53,487 --> 00:02:55,157
Well, you needn't worry.

34
00:02:56,717 --> 00:03:01,717
Wolf and Business Acumen

35
00:03:06,617 --> 00:03:09,257
This town is everything I expected!

36
00:03:10,717 --> 00:03:13,887
It's true. Those are some fine apples.

37
00:03:13,887 --> 00:03:15,107
Right?

38
00:03:17,677 --> 00:03:20,537
They look delicious, no?

39
00:03:24,017 --> 00:03:24,867
Indeed.

40
00:03:25,947 --> 00:03:29,327
Now that I think of it, I had a friend who invested in apples.

41
00:03:29,807 --> 00:03:32,297
He spent half of his life savings.

42
00:03:32,297 --> 00:03:36,337
If they turned out like those, he must have doubled his investment by now.

43
00:03:36,687 --> 00:03:38,427
I should have done the same.

44
00:03:40,317 --> 00:03:42,587
Well... that's most unfortunate...

45
00:03:42,587 --> 00:03:45,097
Then again, the risk would have been high.

46
00:03:45,607 --> 00:03:47,647
I would have transported them by ship.

47
00:03:47,647 --> 00:03:49,017
By... ship, you say?

48
00:03:49,387 --> 00:03:53,647
If you get shipwrecked you might lose your life,
but there's also huge profit to be made.

49
00:03:53,647 --> 00:03:57,897
Sometimes merchants will enter a contract where they all pool some money and rent a ship, and...

50
00:03:58,617 --> 00:03:59,327
What's the matter?

51
00:03:59,327 --> 00:04:00,897
It's nothing.

52
00:04:00,897 --> 00:04:06,897
So once they rent the ship, each merchant can load it with an amount of goods proportional to how much they've invested.

53
00:04:08,137 --> 00:04:09,397
Apples...

54
00:04:09,737 --> 00:04:13,917
I want... to eat... apples...

55
00:04:13,917 --> 00:04:15,917
Oh, is that what you wanted?

56
00:04:20,007 --> 00:04:22,177
Buy as much as you'd like with this.

57
00:04:22,917 --> 00:04:25,047
Who said you could spend all of it?

58
00:04:25,047 --> 00:04:28,247
You're the one who said I could buy as much as I like.

59
00:04:28,967 --> 00:04:31,547
Don't you know the meaning of the word restraint?

60
00:04:32,087 --> 00:04:34,237
You better earn money for your own meals.

61
00:04:34,237 --> 00:04:38,977
I know you pretended not to notice.

62
00:04:39,997 --> 00:04:41,327
Didn't you?

63
00:04:41,327 --> 00:04:45,237
It's amusing knowing what someone else is thinking.

64
00:04:45,237 --> 00:04:46,407
Those are mine!

65
00:04:47,007 --> 00:04:48,307
It was my money!

66
00:04:48,307 --> 00:04:50,367
I'm Holo, the wise wolf.

67
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:53,737
I can make such a petty amount in no time at all.

68
00:04:53,737 --> 00:04:55,487
Oh, glad to hear it!

69
00:04:56,157 --> 00:05:00,257
I was planning to use that money on tonight's room and board.

70
00:05:01,397 --> 00:05:03,007
I'm amazed you ate everything.

71
00:05:03,007 --> 00:05:04,997
Apples are the devil's fruit,

72
00:05:05,307 --> 00:05:08,257
full of tempting sweetness as they are.

73
00:05:08,247 --> 00:05:10,707
Shouldn't a wise wolf be able to conquer temptation?

74
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:16,227
Gluttony may be destructive, but that doesn't mean abstinence is constructive.

75
00:05:18,557 --> 00:05:20,437
That's where we'll do business today.

76
00:05:22,517 --> 00:05:27,987
The entrance may be big, but I think I saw larger buildings than this one.

77
00:05:27,987 --> 00:05:30,987
That's right. It's the third-largest in this town.

78
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:36,757
But it's actually a branch store of a large trading company far to the south.

79
00:05:36,757 --> 00:05:41,167
They don't have local connections, so they pay higher prices to compensate.

80
00:05:41,537 --> 00:05:42,557
More importantly...

81
00:05:42,557 --> 00:05:46,587
All kinds of information come in from their headquarters and other branches, right?

82
00:05:47,077 --> 00:05:52,797
And the fact that they practice trade across borders means
they'll know of any fluctuations in the value of currency.

83
00:05:53,587 --> 00:05:54,687
Exactly.

84
00:05:55,177 --> 00:05:59,187
I'm going to casually ask about Zheren's story.

85
00:05:59,927 --> 00:06:01,727
I may be able to confirm something.

86
00:06:02,347 --> 00:06:04,947
Welcome to Milone Trading!

87
00:06:04,927 --> 00:06:08,317
I sold wheat here three years ago.

88
00:06:08,837 --> 00:06:10,697
I'd like to sell some fur today.

89
00:06:10,997 --> 00:06:13,697
Yes, of course.

90
00:06:13,697 --> 00:06:17,507
Thank you for using our services today.

91
00:06:17,507 --> 00:06:19,497
Mr. Craft Lorentz, was it?

92
00:06:19,777 --> 00:06:21,387
It's Lawrence.

93
00:06:21,387 --> 00:06:23,647
I'm honored that you remembered me.

94
00:06:23,647 --> 00:06:25,677
Not at all. I apologize for the mistake.

95
00:06:25,677 --> 00:06:29,227
I was told that you want to sell fur today.

96
00:06:29,227 --> 00:06:30,257
Correct.

97
00:06:31,377 --> 00:06:33,417
Seventy pelts in all.

98
00:06:33,947 --> 00:06:36,647
This is certainly excellent marten fur.

99
00:06:36,647 --> 00:06:40,397
The supply for marten is scarce due to the fine harvest this year.

100
00:06:40,687 --> 00:06:44,237
The farmers have been too preoccupied to hunt.

101
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:46,397
Yet, here I have a load of the finest of furs.

102
00:06:46,767 --> 00:06:49,657
Seventy in all, was it?

103
00:06:49,657 --> 00:06:50,237
Correct.

104
00:06:50,237 --> 00:06:55,157
We've conducted business with each other
in the past, so how do you feel about this offer?

105
00:06:55,497 --> 00:06:57,087
A hundred and thirty-two, huh?

106
00:06:57,567 --> 00:06:58,457
In which currency?

107
00:06:58,457 --> 00:07:00,047
Trenni silver coins.

108
00:07:02,717 --> 00:07:07,257
You only see furs this fine once every several years... No, make that once every decade.

109
00:07:07,257 --> 00:07:12,467
I'd like to direct your attention to the fact that its shine hasn't faded, despite it being transported through the rain.

110
00:07:12,467 --> 00:07:15,937
It's as you say. The luster is second to none, and the coat has a good lie.

111
00:07:15,937 --> 00:07:19,477
These are furs of a quality rarely seen before.

112
00:07:19,477 --> 00:07:23,857
I'm hoping to keep a good relationship with your company.

113
00:07:23,857 --> 00:07:28,107
As are we, I assure you.

114
00:07:28,097 --> 00:07:32,977
In that case, how about a hundred and forty for the sake of developing that relationship?

115
00:07:34,077 --> 00:07:36,237
Yes, that sounds...

116
00:07:40,237 --> 00:07:41,357
Excuse me a moment.

117
00:07:43,637 --> 00:07:45,467
I don't know the market value.

118
00:07:45,467 --> 00:07:46,567
How's the offer?

119
00:07:46,567 --> 00:07:47,657
It's superb.

120
00:07:51,507 --> 00:07:54,217
In that case, will you accept the offer?

121
00:07:54,217 --> 00:07:57,007
One hundred and forty Trenni silver pieces!

122
00:07:58,477 --> 00:08:00,387
That is what you said, is it not?

123
00:08:01,427 --> 00:08:05,357
Yes, a hundred and forty Trenni silver coins, indeed.

124
00:08:07,587 --> 00:08:10,907
You seem to be a cut above most merchants.

125
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:14,277
Is that why you pretended not to notice?

126
00:08:14,277 --> 00:08:16,787
We'd be wise to be wary of trading with you.

127
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:21,417
I-I beg your pardon. Is there something I may have overlooked?

128
00:08:21,417 --> 00:08:25,127
Master, it's not polite to make sport of people.

129
00:08:26,697 --> 00:08:29,047
T-That was not my aim.

130
00:08:29,657 --> 00:08:31,437
I'll let you explain on my behalf.

131
00:08:34,207 --> 00:08:35,597
Now, sir,

132
00:08:37,217 --> 00:08:39,427
please take the fur in your hands and smell it.

133
00:08:47,347 --> 00:08:48,567
Smell something, do you?

134
00:08:48,927 --> 00:08:51,897
This might be... the scent of fruit, perhaps?

135
00:08:52,687 --> 00:08:53,997
Indeed.

136
00:08:53,997 --> 00:08:57,027
The tree branches drooped with the weight of fruit this year.

137
00:08:57,377 --> 00:09:02,287
These are the furs of marten that have been scampering about in the woods until just recently.

138
00:09:02,287 --> 00:09:07,167
They've been eating lavishly, which is why a sweet fragrance permeates from their bodies.

139
00:09:07,757 --> 00:09:09,047
Yes, I notice the aroma.

140
00:09:09,447 --> 00:09:11,557
These are furs from the finest marten.

141
00:09:11,557 --> 00:09:17,297
It took two grown men to flay the hide from the body, it was so tough.

142
00:09:18,077 --> 00:09:21,187
Don't be reserved. Pull it with all your strength.

143
00:09:23,137 --> 00:09:24,087
Harder.

144
00:09:25,837 --> 00:09:31,487
The fur is as strong as the beast itself was, and the warmth it provides is like sunshine on a spring day.

145
00:09:31,487 --> 00:09:36,117
It will repel rain from dawn 'til dusk,
and don't forget the scent!

146
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:39,277
Imagine coming across a perfumed piece like this

147
00:09:39,277 --> 00:09:44,297
among coats made from nose-wrinkling marten fur.

148
00:09:44,297 --> 00:09:47,417
Why, 'twould sell so dear your eyes would pop out.

149
00:09:48,287 --> 00:09:52,257
Now then! What price will you offer?

150
00:09:54,827 --> 00:09:58,007
How about two hundred Trenni silver coins?

151
00:10:01,307 --> 00:10:04,687
How does three pieces of silver per fur sound?

152
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:05,877
Two hundred and ten in all.

153
00:10:06,567 --> 00:10:07,597
Well...

154
00:10:08,187 --> 00:10:10,067
Master, aren't there other trading companies?

155
00:10:11,317 --> 00:10:14,827
Very well. Two hundred and ten pieces it is.

156
00:10:15,997 --> 00:10:18,407
You heard him, master.

157
00:10:20,627 --> 00:10:21,537
Yeah...

158
00:10:24,437 --> 00:10:25,907
Cheers!

159
00:10:32,087 --> 00:10:33,967
Nothing beats the taste of good wine!

160
00:10:34,827 --> 00:10:37,517
What's the matter? Are you not going to drink?

161
00:10:37,517 --> 00:10:39,477
It's my treat.

162
00:10:39,477 --> 00:10:42,597
Have you ever worked as a merchant?

163
00:10:42,597 --> 00:10:46,807
What is it? Did my actions wound your pride or something?

164
00:10:46,807 --> 00:10:51,607
Well, I do not quite remember when, but that idea dates from a long time ago.

165
00:10:52,217 --> 00:10:56,527
A clever merchant who was passing through the village came up with it.

166
00:10:57,267 --> 00:11:00,127
It wasn't something I came up with myself.

167
00:11:09,117 --> 00:11:11,447
I really hadn't noticed, though.

168
00:11:11,447 --> 00:11:16,297
Actually, even last night when I slept in the furs, I didn't smell any fruit.

169
00:11:16,707 --> 00:11:19,757
Well, of course not. It's because of the apples I bought earlier.

170
00:11:20,377 --> 00:11:21,807
In other words...

171
00:11:21,807 --> 00:11:23,557
It's his own fault for being tricked!

172
00:11:23,937 --> 00:11:28,817
Well, maybe not, but I'm sure he'll be impressed and glad to learn of the truth.

173
00:11:28,817 --> 00:11:30,397
I suppose.

174
00:11:30,397 --> 00:11:34,107
It's fruitless to be incensed after being deceived.

175
00:11:34,757 --> 00:11:38,987
Being able to be impressed and learn is what makes an adult.

176
00:11:39,677 --> 00:11:43,367
So, did you find the other thing you were looking for?

177
00:11:44,197 --> 00:11:45,197
After a fashion.

178
00:11:45,667 --> 00:11:49,957
They haven't heard any rumors about a country that's planning to renew its currency.

179
00:11:54,117 --> 00:11:58,947
Well, whatever the trick with Zheren's story,

180
00:11:58,947 --> 00:12:01,537
I don't mind as long as there's a profit to be made.

181
00:12:02,297 --> 00:12:05,007
Here's to our reunion.

182
00:12:05,007 --> 00:12:05,997
Cheers!

183
00:12:11,217 --> 00:12:16,147
Being able to drink such wonderful wine must mean you sold the furs for a good price, right?

184
00:12:16,147 --> 00:12:16,927
More or less.

185
00:12:16,927 --> 00:12:20,647
That's great! More capital means more profit for me!

186
00:12:21,327 --> 00:12:23,467
More importantly...

187
00:12:23,467 --> 00:12:24,157
Yes?

188
00:12:24,817 --> 00:12:28,587
In exchange for information regarding the currency that's going to be reissued,

189
00:12:28,587 --> 00:12:32,087
you want a percentage of my profits.

190
00:12:32,087 --> 00:12:33,477
That sums it up, correct?

191
00:12:33,477 --> 00:12:34,227
Yes.

192
00:12:34,227 --> 00:12:36,877
Can your information be trusted?

193
00:12:37,707 --> 00:12:44,887
Well, I'm predicting it based off snippets I heard in a mining camp.

194
00:12:44,887 --> 00:12:47,337
I think it's trustworthy.

195
00:12:47,337 --> 00:12:48,607
However...

196
00:12:49,377 --> 00:12:51,887
There are no guarantees in business.

197
00:12:55,847 --> 00:12:58,447
I would have walked away if you had said it was a sure thing.

198
00:12:58,447 --> 00:13:00,497
Nothing is more suspicious than a guarantee.

199
00:13:01,437 --> 00:13:03,217
What percentage did you want?

200
00:13:03,217 --> 00:13:06,977
Oh, right. I'd like ten Trenni pieces for the information.

201
00:13:06,977 --> 00:13:10,577
Plus ten percent of your profit, sir.

202
00:13:10,577 --> 00:13:12,737
That's a rather modest amount.

203
00:13:12,737 --> 00:13:17,037
Well, there's nothing I can do for you in the event of a loss.

204
00:13:17,347 --> 00:13:24,947
I'll take just ten percent, but if you lose everything, I'll refund the information fee and no more.

205
00:13:24,947 --> 00:13:26,967
That sounds good enough to me.

206
00:13:26,967 --> 00:13:28,507
Thank you very much.

207
00:13:28,917 --> 00:13:32,017
In that case, can we visit the notary public tomorrow?

208
00:13:34,267 --> 00:13:36,017
To our profit.

209
00:13:36,627 --> 00:13:37,757
To our profit!

210
00:13:38,767 --> 00:13:39,947
Cheers!

211
00:13:44,267 --> 00:13:45,607
Farum silver coin!

212
00:13:45,607 --> 00:13:47,897
Wrong. It's a counterfeit Marinne silver coin.

213
00:13:47,897 --> 00:13:49,527
Is that not this one?

214
00:13:49,877 --> 00:13:52,197
That's a later version of Bishop Radeon silver coin.

215
00:13:53,697 --> 00:13:56,437
Well, you'll learn quickly once you start using them.

216
00:13:56,437 --> 00:13:58,197
Let's continue once we're sober.

217
00:13:58,197 --> 00:13:59,667
No, one more time!

218
00:14:00,187 --> 00:14:01,847
As you wish.

219
00:14:01,847 --> 00:14:04,327
I'm going to start from here. Pay close attention.

220
00:14:04,327 --> 00:14:05,177
Okay.

221
00:14:05,637 --> 00:14:08,687
Trenni silver coin, Philing silver coin,

222
00:14:08,687 --> 00:14:11,927
Lute silver coin, counterfeit Marinne silver coin,

223
00:14:12,317 --> 00:14:15,437
Farum silver coin, Bald King Ranbalt silver coin,

224
00:14:15,437 --> 00:14:17,527
Mitzfing Cathedral silver coin,

225
00:14:17,527 --> 00:14:19,927
counterfeit Mitzfing Cathedral silver coin,

226
00:14:19,927 --> 00:14:23,597
St. Mitzfing silver coin, and last but not least...

227
00:14:23,597 --> 00:14:25,537
I've had enough. I'm going to bed.

228
00:14:25,537 --> 00:14:27,697
A decision befitting a wise wolf.

229
00:14:28,897 --> 00:14:31,587
Why are there so many of them to begin with?

230
00:14:31,587 --> 00:14:33,727
It's too confusing.

231
00:14:33,727 --> 00:14:37,217
It's due to the endless cycle of countries rising and falling.

232
00:14:37,217 --> 00:14:41,587
Also, rural authorities and leaders involved with the church reissue currency at will.

233
00:14:41,587 --> 00:14:43,507
Add counterfeits to the mix, and, well...

234
00:14:44,027 --> 00:14:47,907
Actually, Lute silver coins were originally called counterfeit Trenni silver coins, and...

235
00:14:49,227 --> 00:14:50,297
Don't fall asleep on me.

236
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:06,827
I'll make good use of this information.

237
00:15:07,477 --> 00:15:08,487
You have my gratitude.

238
00:15:09,117 --> 00:15:10,157
Thank you very much.

239
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:13,247
I'll be on my way, sir.

240
00:15:13,247 --> 00:15:13,987
Okay.

241
00:15:13,987 --> 00:15:17,327
Make a killing, sir!

242
00:15:17,637 --> 00:15:20,167
Stay beautiful, madam!

243
00:15:23,367 --> 00:15:25,667
He was noisy right to the very end.

244
00:15:27,657 --> 00:15:30,137
This is the silver coin in question, isn't it?

245
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:30,677
Yeah.

246
00:15:31,147 --> 00:15:33,977
It's a credible form of currency in this area.

247
00:15:33,977 --> 00:15:35,357
Credible?

248
00:15:35,357 --> 00:15:40,687
There are several hundred currencies in existence, and the
amount of gold or silver often fluctuates in many of them.

249
00:15:41,047 --> 00:15:45,747
Basically, the value of money is much greater than the amount of gold or silver it contains.

250
00:15:45,747 --> 00:15:48,117
That extra value comes from trust.

251
00:15:48,117 --> 00:15:49,927
I see.

252
00:15:50,407 --> 00:15:54,667
Is there anything you've learned now that you know this is the coin?

253
00:15:54,667 --> 00:15:55,697
Well...

254
00:15:56,437 --> 00:15:59,417
I might not know all the details, but I have an idea.

255
00:16:02,797 --> 00:16:03,867
What's the matter?

256
00:16:03,867 --> 00:16:05,717
I want to eat one of those.

257
00:16:05,717 --> 00:16:06,627
Those?

258
00:16:11,317 --> 00:16:14,477
So, what did you realize?

259
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,757
Do you remember which coin this is?

260
00:16:19,417 --> 00:16:21,277
Philing silver coin?

261
00:16:21,277 --> 00:16:22,767
Correct.

262
00:16:22,767 --> 00:16:26,567
Its silver content is extremely high,
and it's popular in the marketplace.

263
00:16:26,567 --> 00:16:28,787
It rivals the Trenni coin in that respect.

264
00:16:28,787 --> 00:16:32,477
It seems the strength of a country is reflected in its currency in every age.

265
00:16:32,477 --> 00:16:37,867
Right. When the local market is dominated by a foreign
currency, the economy will become dependent on it.

266
00:16:37,867 --> 00:16:39,267
It's no different from losing a war.

267
00:16:39,567 --> 00:16:43,947
In order to defeat a rival's currency, you have to increase the purity of your own coins, right?

268
00:16:44,807 --> 00:16:49,207
Yeah, which is why Zheren may not be lying about the situation.

269
00:16:49,207 --> 00:16:51,887
It's true that my ears aren't completely flawless.

270
00:16:52,837 --> 00:16:56,097
What? Did you think I was going to be angry?

271
00:16:56,097 --> 00:16:56,847
I sure did.

272
00:16:57,627 --> 00:17:00,677
I may get upset about you thinking that way, though.

273
00:17:02,817 --> 00:17:04,777
Where are we going?

274
00:17:04,777 --> 00:17:06,857
I happen to know a money changer.

275
00:17:06,857 --> 00:17:08,937
A money changer?

276
00:17:08,937 --> 00:17:12,717
A small change to a coin's purity would be impossible for a layman to detect.

277
00:17:12,717 --> 00:17:16,937
Yet a big reason why coin value fluctuates is that people care about changes in purity.

278
00:17:16,937 --> 00:17:20,947
People see minor changes as precursors to major ones.

279
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:25,247
That's why there's always a precursor before a big change.

280
00:17:27,187 --> 00:17:29,177
You don't have to learn all of this at once.

281
00:17:29,177 --> 00:17:32,177
I'll gradually explain it to you over the next month.

282
00:17:32,177 --> 00:17:33,547
In other words,

283
00:17:33,547 --> 00:17:37,307
when a mint decides to drastically change the purity,

284
00:17:37,307 --> 00:17:41,177
they first increase it by a small fraction to gauge public reaction.

285
00:17:41,177 --> 00:17:44,307
Depending on the reaction, they wait for an appropriate time to increase its value.

286
00:17:45,217 --> 00:17:48,187
Y-Yeah. Something like that.

287
00:17:49,867 --> 00:17:50,647
Lawrence!

288
00:17:50,647 --> 00:17:51,727
Weiz!

289
00:17:51,727 --> 00:17:54,157
Long time no see!

290
00:17:54,157 --> 00:17:55,327
Come on.

291
00:17:55,327 --> 00:17:57,037
Young lady, who might you be?

292
00:17:57,037 --> 00:17:58,707
Me?

293
00:17:58,707 --> 00:18:00,667
My name is Holo.

294
00:18:00,667 --> 00:18:02,657
Holo! What a wonderful name.

295
00:18:03,277 --> 00:18:05,717
Lawrence, have you slept with her yet?

296
00:18:05,717 --> 00:18:07,317
Of course not!

297
00:18:07,317 --> 00:18:08,627
So she's fair game, then?

298
00:18:10,547 --> 00:18:11,887
May I have the honor?

299
00:18:14,107 --> 00:18:15,777
I-I don't know...

300
00:18:20,417 --> 00:18:22,137
My business with you comes first.

301
00:18:22,717 --> 00:18:25,727
Do you have any recently-issued Trenni silver coins?

302
00:18:27,327 --> 00:18:28,517
There's no way.

303
00:18:29,127 --> 00:18:32,197
We handle it every day, but we haven't noticed anything.

304
00:18:32,197 --> 00:18:34,137
Do you want to melt it down and find out?

305
00:18:34,137 --> 00:18:36,237
Don't be ridiculous! There's no way we could do that.

306
00:18:36,787 --> 00:18:38,727
Could I take a look?

307
00:18:38,727 --> 00:18:40,527
Please, be my guest!

308
00:18:44,087 --> 00:18:45,957
You're a wicked man.

309
00:18:48,297 --> 00:18:49,747
Well, just watch.

310
00:18:53,457 --> 00:18:55,807
I don't think it's possible to distinguish them like that, Miss Holo.

311
00:18:56,537 --> 00:19:00,747
I've heard that some money changers who've worked for decades can do that,

312
00:19:00,747 --> 00:19:02,557
but those are just legends.

313
00:19:05,367 --> 00:19:06,327
What do you think?

314
00:19:08,547 --> 00:19:09,947
I can't tell.

315
00:19:11,397 --> 00:19:13,527
Oh, too bad! Too bad, indeed!

316
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,067
Don't worry about it.

317
00:19:15,717 --> 00:19:17,367
He was interesting, wasn't he?

318
00:19:17,367 --> 00:19:19,047
He's a womanizer without peer.

319
00:19:20,427 --> 00:19:24,457
So, did the silver content increase or decrease?

320
00:19:25,117 --> 00:19:27,867
If that was just a guess, then you've gotten much more sly.

321
00:19:28,267 --> 00:19:30,577
I noticed a slight movement in your ears.

322
00:19:30,577 --> 00:19:32,297
Can't let my guard down.

323
00:19:32,297 --> 00:19:35,677
I was surprised you didn't say anything back there.

324
00:19:35,677 --> 00:19:37,767
Well, think of it as an act of compensation.

325
00:19:37,767 --> 00:19:38,837
Compensation?

326
00:19:38,837 --> 00:19:41,467
You were a little jealous, weren't you?

327
00:19:41,467 --> 00:19:42,967
This is in exchange.

328
00:19:44,367 --> 00:19:46,357
Don't make such a worried face.

329
00:19:46,357 --> 00:19:49,527
All men burn with foolish jealousy,

330
00:19:49,527 --> 00:19:52,267
and women are foolish enough to take delight in it.

331
00:19:52,267 --> 00:19:53,977
The world is full of fools.

332
00:19:54,867 --> 00:19:56,467
Wait. What about the silver?

333
00:19:57,717 --> 00:20:01,477
It was subtle, but the new coins sounded dull in comparison.

334
00:20:01,857 --> 00:20:03,107
Dull?

335
00:20:03,107 --> 00:20:05,987
That means that its purity has decreased.

336
00:20:06,787 --> 00:20:08,997
So Zheren really was lying?

337
00:20:09,827 --> 00:20:12,997
You can only make long-term profits from a depreciating currency.

338
00:20:12,997 --> 00:20:16,497
If you sell your coins and buy them back after the price drops, you'll end up with more.

339
00:20:17,127 --> 00:20:19,717
There's a profit to be made once the price recovers,

340
00:20:19,717 --> 00:20:22,257
but six months isn't enough time.

341
00:20:22,257 --> 00:20:25,927
There has to be another way for Zheren to profit.

342
00:20:29,367 --> 00:20:31,857
Have you not been tricked?

343
00:20:31,857 --> 00:20:32,947
Tricked?

344
00:20:32,947 --> 00:20:34,567
That's right.

345
00:20:34,567 --> 00:20:38,067
Do you mean I was swindled out of the ten silver coins?

346
00:20:38,067 --> 00:20:40,157
In the worst-case scenario, the boy breaks even.

347
00:20:40,157 --> 00:20:43,457
Even if the value of the silver coin depreciates and you face losses,

348
00:20:43,457 --> 00:20:46,077
all that young man has to do is return the information fee.

349
00:20:46,727 --> 00:20:49,367
But he'll receive a share of your profit, if there is any.

350
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:55,977
He's in a position to make a profit without any capital and won't incur any losses.

351
00:20:56,627 --> 00:20:58,127
Oh my God.

352
00:20:59,337 --> 00:21:01,177
Human beings are ingenious.

353
00:21:01,177 --> 00:21:02,597
Oh my God.

354
00:21:03,877 --> 00:21:04,957
However,

355
00:21:05,897 --> 00:21:10,227
is it normal for there to be a decrease in a coin's silver content?

356
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:14,397
No, normally the purity is maintained with extreme care.

357
00:21:15,677 --> 00:21:21,117
A deal that hinges on the purity of this particular coin has come out of nowhere. Is that just a coincidence?

358
00:21:21,737 --> 00:21:26,227
When we hunt, we occasionally climb trees.

359
00:21:26,237 --> 00:21:30,457
We're able to see hidden lairs of our prey from that vantage point.

360
00:21:30,457 --> 00:21:33,507
It's necessary to change your perspective in times like these.

361
00:21:34,257 --> 00:21:36,467
Change my perspective?

362
00:21:36,467 --> 00:21:41,257
What if the person behind this scheme wasn't that young man?

363
00:21:42,077 --> 00:21:47,207
That young man's profit doesn't necessarily have to come from the people he tricked.

364
00:21:47,827 --> 00:21:53,707
He could have been asked to spread news about a suspicious deal in return for a service fee.

365
00:21:53,707 --> 00:21:55,807
That's it! I understand everything!

366
00:21:56,137 --> 00:21:59,607
There's a way to make a profit by buying as much of a depreciating currency as you can!

367
00:22:00,567 --> 00:22:02,447
Looks like something clicked.

368
00:22:02,447 --> 00:22:03,237
Let's go!

369
00:22:04,817 --> 00:22:06,747
Where are we going?

370
00:22:06,747 --> 00:22:08,207
Milone Trading.

371
00:23:40,847 --> 00:23:44,157
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and the Helpless Partner."</i>

372
00:23:44,537 --> 00:23:46,537


373
00:23:45,857 --> 00:23:49,157
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and the Helpless Partner."</i>

